Push a change to this file (any change, for example bump the number below) to rebuild Leaf/Resources/catalog.sqlite
from the latest Open Library data dumps. The "Catalog" workflow (.github/workflows/catalog.yml) does the work and, only if
every sanity check passes, commits the new database to main as "Catalog: rebuild (N books)". It takes about one to
two hours. Nothing else triggers it: editing other files never starts a rebuild, and the workflow's own commit does not
touch this file, so it can never loop.

You can also start it by hand: GitHub, Actions, Catalog, Run workflow (optionally pin a dump date such as 2026-09-30).

Rebuild requests so far: 3 (2026-10-22: ISBNs for offline barcode scans; more ISBNs for the most read; erotica left out)
